WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.103
-We do not always
have enough time

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.505
to cover everything going on
with recent news.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.674
So here with a recap is one
of our writers, Amber Ruffin,

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:10.943
in a segment we call
"Amber Says What."

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:13.813
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:17.350
-You guys!
Things have been crazy!

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.820
Okay, first of all,
the U.S. Open began last week,

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.655
and I was like, "What?"

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:27.527
Then I saw Serena's outfit,
and I was like, "What?"

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:30.930
Then Serena hurt her ankle,
and I was like, "Oh, no.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.632
Is the outfit okay?"

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.066
And it was.

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:36.035
Serena was amazing.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.771
She beat Karolina.
She beat Petra.

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:42.107
And she beat Qiang so fast
that I was like, "Wha--"

00:00:42.107 --> 00:00:45.277
'cause I didn't get time
to get out a whole "what."

00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:48.581
Then Naomi Osaka
played Coco Gauff,

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.684
and after Naomi beat Coco,
she comforted her.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:54.220
And I was like, "What?"

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.189
Then I was like,
"It's okay, Coco.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.857
You have plenty of time
to win stuff.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.659
You're probably
only 20 years old."

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:03.196
And then someone was like,
"She's 15 years old."

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:05.464
And I was like, "What?"

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:08.534
Because when people that age
accomplish big things,

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:11.704
it makes people my age
feel bad about themselves.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:16.108
And if you ask me what my age
is, I would say, "What?"

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:18.544
Because my hearing is also bad.

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:21.214
Because I am very old.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:23.482
I'm 22.

00:01:23.482 --> 00:01:27.286
Then I found out men also play
at the U.S. Open,

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:29.389
and I was like, "What?"

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:33.392
No shade. It had honestly never
occurred to me that they might.

00:01:33.392 --> 00:01:37.764
Then I heard everyone was
talking about the salmon cannon.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.699
And I was like, "What?"

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:40.766
Salmon cannon?

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:43.235
You guys don't have to
make weapons

00:01:43.235 --> 00:01:45.571
just because Trump
thinks them up.

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:48.241
Then people were like,
"That's not what this is.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:51.410
This is a tube
that shoots salmon

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:55.181
so their lazy behinds
don't have to swim upstream."

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.817
And I was like, "What?"

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.652
I liked it better as a weapon.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:00.986
Now, hear me out.

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:04.424
You shoot a salmon at
your enemy, and he'd be like,

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:08.827
"You hit me with a yummy fish
that's high in omega-3.

00:02:08.827 --> 00:02:11.430
You are no longer my enemy.
You're my friend."

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.066
Everyone wins.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:17.337
Then I heard that rap label
Death Row Records

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.271
was bought by a company,
and I was like,

00:02:19.271 --> 00:02:24.077
"What's my mother[bleep] name?"

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:28.180
Then I was like,
"What company is tough enough

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.648
to buy Death Row?

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:31.451
Is it Interscope Records?

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.086
Is it Jay-Z's streaming service,
Tidal?"

00:02:34.086 --> 00:02:38.824
Then I found out it was Hasbro.

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:40.026
This is real.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:43.062
The toy company Hasbro
bought Death Row Records.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.431
I was like, "What?"

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:49.135
My two favorite things
together at last.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:52.137
My Little Ponies and Tupac.

00:02:52.137 --> 00:02:55.341
They'll finally be able
to make my dream pony,

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.610
Princess Makaveli.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.713
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:04.851
Makaveli is Tupac's nickname,
and if you don't know that,

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.152
there's nothing I can do
to help you.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.954
Also, he's still alive.

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:10.923
Then, in other toy news,

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:14.560
Mattel came out with
a Rosa Parks Barbie!

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.731
And I was like, "What?"

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:25.138
A real-life -- A real-life
activist gets their own Barbie?

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:26.105
Sweet!

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.940
Then the website was like,

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.877
"She led an ordinary life
as a seamstress

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:33.045
until one extraordinary moment."

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:36.215
And I was like, "Wait."
That's wrong.

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:37.884
She was a member of the NAACP

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.286
and she enacted
a well-thought-out plan.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.855
Black people didn't accidentally
end up with rights.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.357
People worked hard to get them.

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:47.360
That's like releasing
a Martin Luther King doll

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.595
and saying,
"He was an ordinary guy

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:54.033
until he accidentally
ended up at a podium."

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:57.536
"I have a dream?"

00:03:57.536 --> 00:04:01.708
Then 17-year-old Swedish
activist Greta Thunberg

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:04.677
took a boat across
the Atlantic Ocean

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:08.213
to draw attention to climate
change, and I was like, "What?"

00:04:08.213 --> 00:04:10.049
17?

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.884
What are the rules?

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:14.220
So you're telling me
a 17-year-old

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.988
can travel across the ocean

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:18.758
and a 15-year-old
can be in the U.S. Open?

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:20.959
Next you're going to tell me
a 22-year-old

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:23.329
can have her own segment
on a late-night talk show.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.832
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:30.302 --> 00:04:34.907
Then a White House aide
said Pence couldn't be anti-gay

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:36.943
because he's going to
have lunch this week

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:39.078
with the openly gay
prime minister of Ireland

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.212
and his partner.

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:42.381
And I was like, "What?"

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:44.483
Okay, just because
you spend an hour

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:47.787
in the same room with someone
does not mean you respect them.

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:51.190
My therapist hates my guts.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.026
And also, I got major beef

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:55.928
with this show's
camera assistant Kenny,

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.197
and we work together every day.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:01.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.616
This has been "Amber Says What."

00:05:17.616 --> 00:05:19.552
[ Cheers and applause ]

